  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 厚\ntitle: thick; cordial\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 厂\nradicalNumber: 27\nonyomi: [コウ]\nkunyomi: [あつ.い, あか]\ndistractors: [原, 屋, 度]\n---\n\n# 厚 — thick; cordial\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 厂 (no. 27) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n厚 expresses physical thickness in 厚い あつい. It also occurs in kindness or cordial treatment, as in 厚意 こうい, kindness shown by someone else. A thick book and a kind favor are different uses, not a literal claim that kindness has a measurable thickness.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Imagine a thick stack beneath the 厂 overhang, with a 日-like box above 子. This is a way to remember the present outline.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| コウ | on | 厚意 こうい - kindness shown by others; courtesy |\n| あつ.い | kun | [厚い](../words/厚い.md) あつい - thick |\n| あか | kun | Source-only reading; see the qualification below. |\n\nKANJIDIC2 also records `あか`. No suitable word example was established in the inspected JMdict snapshot. These are character-dictionary readings for lookup, not recommendations to use this kanji as an everyday spelling of a word.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [厚い](../words/厚い.md) あつい - thick\n- [厚かましい](../words/厚かましい.md) あつかましい - brazen; shameless\n- 厚意 こうい - kindness shown by others; courtesy\n\n## Notes\n\n- Distinguish 厚い あつい, thick, from 暑い あつい, hot weather, and 熱い あつい, hot to the touch or intensely felt. The sound alone does not choose the spelling.\n- 厚意 is not a claim about the physical thickness of a person or object.\n- The additional source reading あか is retained for lookup, not taught here as an ordinary way to say thick or red.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1275320, 1275330, 1275370.\n",
